      "why": "then run the restack again: it records feat-y where you put it and goes on with the features above it",
      "needs_human": false,
      "needs_input": []
    }
  ],
  "error": {
    "code": "REBASE_CONFLICT",
    "message": "feat-y does not restack cleanly onto feat-x: commit <SHA2:12> stopped on conflicts in feature.txt. The branches restacked before it stay restacked, and feat-y is unchanged; Ghostbranch never resolves conflicts: rebase it yourself (details.steps), push it, then run ghostbranch feature restack feat-x",
    "field": "feature",
    "retryable": false,
    "details": {
      "again": [
        "feature",
        "restack",
        "feat-x"
